{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p1-e3e201d8","text":"The elevation request timed out (not approved/denied — timed out). I should fall back to the junction patch in node_modules (no admin needed). Actually — first, I left a debug patch in copyTracedFiles.js (I added console.error line). I need to restore/modify it properly.

Plan: patch copyTracedFiles.js to fall back to a junction (or copy) when symlinkSync throws EPERM. Junctions don't require admin for directories. Target must be absolute — it is.

Patch:
```js
if (symlink) {
    try {
        symlinkSync(symlink, to);
    }
    catch (e) {
        if (e.code === "EPERM" || e.code === "EACCES") {
            // Windows without Developer Mode: directory junctions need no privilege
            symlinkSync(symlink, to, "junction");
        } else if (e.code !== "EEXIST") {
            throw e;
        }
    }
}
```

Careful: junction target must be absolute — symlink value here is absolute (`C:\files\...`). Good. But note the symlink may also be created for FILE symlinks in other cases — junction only works for dirs; if it fails again it throws.

Also note: my debug console.error line should be removed in the same patch.

Caveat: node_modules patch is wiped on reinstall. Document this to the user. Alternative would be elevation (timed out).

Wait — also consider: sites_prepare_next might reinstall packages on each run (first run added 304 packages). If it reinstalls, patch is lost. Let's patch, then run sites_prepare_next and see.

Actually — maybe better alternative: make the SOURCE not a symlink. The source is created by Next build at `.next/standalone/.next/node_modules/<pkg>-hash`. Could we make OpenNext not traverse... no.

Or: `OPEN_NEXT_*` env vars? There's OPEN_NEXT_SKIP_PLATFORM_FILTER only.

Hmm, what about npm config to make... no.

Another thought: could we disable the symlink creation by Next? The symlink at `.next/standalone/.next/node_modules/@electric-sql/pglite-7966c14983af6418` — why does Next create it? Because of serverExternalPackages — Next copies external packages into standalone and creates symlinks when the package already exists in standalone/node_modules (dedupe by content hash). If pglite weren't in serverExternalPackages... it would be bundled (breaks). 

Alternatively, does Next create symlinks only when `experimental.serverSourceMaps`...? Unknown. Not worth deep investigation.

Also — is there maybe an env var or flag: `--experimental-build-mode`... no.

Go with junction fallback patch. Also verify git status doesn't include node_modules (it's gitignored).

